truction, impermeability tests; drilling of deep wells; pilot plant"},{"method":"seismic","page":144,"text":"A total of 62,500 m of seismic survey data was acquired. The survey configuration utilized a five-metre geophone separation, and a semi-logarithmic expanding drop-weight source","year":2009},{"method":"gravity","page":147,"text":"-101 Technical Report Cauchari-Olaroz Salars, Argentina Page 124 of 555 9.4 GRAVITY SURVEY A reconnaissance gravity survey was completed at the Cauchari Salar during July of 2010.","year":2026,"platform":"borehole"},{"method":"gravity","page":148,"text":"Cauchari-Olaroz Salars, Argentina Page 125 of 555 FIGURE 9.3 LOCATION OF GRAVITY SURVEY LINES AT THE CAUCHARI SALAR Source: Burga et al.","year":2026},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":151,"text":"the survey was to test the applicability of this method for determining resistivity contrasts that may relate to changes in groundwater salinity."},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":151,"text":"Salars, Argentina Page 128 of 555 9.5 TEM SURVEY A Time Domain Electromagnetic (TEM) survey was conducted in the Cauchari Salar during July 2010, along the five TEM lines shown in Figure 9.6.","year":2026},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":155,"text":"The resistivity values suggest continuity of the brine to surface. Below 65 m the lithology is characterized by high halite content.","platform":"borehole"},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":156,"text":"The central portion of the inversion shows an area of higher resistivity extending from the surface to a depth of approximately 75 m. Laterally, this zone could approach one kilometre in width.","platform":"ground"},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":281,"text":"surveys conducted using Vertical Electrical Soundings (VES), Transient Electromagnetics (TEM), and Audiomagnetotelluric (AMT) methods.","year":2025},{"method":"magnetotellurics","page":281,"text":"The Leapfrog model developed by Montgomery (2025) was further updated through the current work, to support Resource Estimat","year":2025},{"method":"seismic","page":404,"text":"prior updates and encompassing planned exploration activities, including seismic reflection, hydrogeological studies, pond construction, and geochemical sampling. \u2022 2020 Update: Approved by Resolution No.","year":2017}],"targets":[]},"rock":null,"model_params":{"block":[100.0,100.0,25.0],"density":2.65,"top_cut":100.0,"method":"idw","power":2.0,"metallurgy":{"routes":[],"traits":["transitional","clay"],"recoveries":{"Li2O":75.0},"summary":"transitional ore present, clay-rich; stated recovery Li2O 75%"},"deposit_style":"pegmatite"},"effective_date":"2026-09-15","resource":null,"resource_rows":[],"counts":{"collars":106,"intervals":0,"surveyed_holes":0,"holes_with_intervals":0,"linked":0},"collars":[{"hole":"DD17S-001","e":3424377.0,"n":7378282.0,"z":null,"az":null,"dip":null,"depth":50.0},{"hole":"DD17D-001","e":3424392.0,"n":7378275.0,"z":null,"az":null,"dip":null,"depth":450.0},{"hole":"DD17D-002B","e":3427266.0,"n":7396185.0,"z":null,"az":null,"dip":null,"depth":450.0},{"hole":"DD17S-002","e":3427273.0,"n":7396180.0,"z":null,"az":null,"dip":null,"depth":50.0},{"hole":"DD17S-003","e":3430870.0,"n":7404487.0,"z":null,"az":null,"dip":null,"depth":200.0},{"hole":"DD17D-003","e":3430861.0,"n":7404476.0,"z":null,"az":null,"dip":null,"depth":650.0},{"hole":"RC17D-003","e":3430859.0,"n":7404497.0,"z":null,"az":null,"dip":null,"depth":648.0},{"hole":"RC17S-004","e":3422991.0,"n":7379367.0,"z":null,"az":null,"dip":null,"depth":50.0},{"hole":"DD17D-004","e":3423010.0,"n":7379367.0,"z":null,"az":null,"dip":null,"depth":650.0},{"hole":"RC17D-004 B","e":3423006.0,"n":7379355.0,"z":null,"az":null,"dip":null,"depth":550.0},{"hole":"RC17S-004 B","e":3423001.0,"n":7379362.0,"z":null,"az":null,"dip":null,"depth":50.0},{"hole":"DD17D-005","e":3429086.0,"n":7400627.0,"z":null,"az":null,"dip":null,"depth":604.55},{"hole":"RC17S-005","e":3429092.0,"n":7400696.0,"z":null,"az":null,"dip":null,"depth":192.